  "notes": "{憎悪|ぞうお} is a formal, literary word expressing intense hatred or loathing—stronger than everyday words like ⟦{嫌|きら}い→嫌い：02871_kirai⟧.\n\nUSAGE AS VERB:\n{憎悪|ぞうお}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to hate intensely, to loathe\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {憎悪|ぞうお}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{抱|いだ}く→抱く：02010_idaku⟧: to harbor hatred\n- {憎悪|ぞうお}⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{満|み}ちた→満ちる：02428_michiru⟧: filled with hatred\n- {憎悪|ぞうお}⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{生|う}まれる→生まれる：00905_umareru⟧: hatred arises\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {憎悪|ぞうお}⟦{犯罪|はんざい}→犯罪：03569_hanzai⟧: hate crime\n- ⟦{人種|じんしゅ}→人種：03354_jinshu⟧{憎悪|ぞうお}: racial hatred\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {憎悪|ぞうお}: intense hatred (formal, literary)\n- ⟦{憎|にく}む→憎む：00318_nikumu⟧: to hate (neutral verb)\n- ⟦{嫌|きら}い→嫌い：02871_kirai⟧: dislike (casual)\n- ⟦{恨|うら}み→恨み：00414_urami⟧: grudge, resentment",
